# v3b (2026-10-14): TSS (pTracer 36) = 0 on inflow (python/make_tss_obcs.py). Without OB?ptrFile(36)
# obcs_calc.F copies the adjacent interior TSS onto the boundary every step, so tidal inflow carried
# resuspended sediment back in: net open-boundary import 5.9e14 g by day 180 in v3 (S5 5.5e13 g) vs an
# initial domain total of 2.3e11 g (%SEDIMENT_MON). Tracers 33-35 (kelp) keep the default.
 &OBCS_PARM01
 OB_Iwest = 72*1,
 OB_Ieast = 72*-1,
 OB_Jsouth = 128*1,
 useOBCSprescribe = .TRUE.,
 useOBCSsponge = .TRUE.,
 useOBCSbalance = .TRUE.,
# v3 (2026-10-13): tides through the OBs (build_tides: ALLOW_OBCS_TIDES, 2-day ramp), added to the normal
# flow after OBCS_BALANCE_FLOW. Amplitudes/phases of M2,S2,N2,K2,K1,O1,P1,Q1 from the socal tidal run
# run_v3_prod hourly transports (python/socal_tides_malibu.py; K2/P1 ride on S2/K1 with the socal
# OB ratios); phase zero = 2025-01-01, nodal factors of Jan-Jun 2025.
